abstract: >-
  A speculative hypothesis treating the universe as a globally conserved
  informational structure, where cosmological cycles correspond to changes in
  local information readability rather than temporal restarts. Version 0.1.5
  consolidates a bounded finite-time selector counterexample, a fixed-protocol
  observational-entropy comparison, and its local measurement implementation.
  The entangled strict local minimum is not globally preferred and is
  outperformed in the stipulated recovery task. Measurement statistics do not
  establish coherent subsystem control, a physical entropy reset, or algebra
  selection. Earlier EC/CAR robustness and specificity failures are unchanged.
  The finite-example sequence is closed; cosmological selection, effective
  entropy, transition dynamics, and observational predictions remain open.
